one of the great things about the visual  effects branch is that we have what's  called a bake-off every year and what  happens is that there is a group of the  effects people in the branch who  determine what we call the long list  there's seven films that are that are  chosen and then those films are  presented to the entire visual effects  branch and the entire visual effects  branch views 20 minute clips from each  of those films that are put together by  the filmmakers the visual effects  supervisor typically gets up and has  some opening and closing remarks to help  explain what you're looking at but we  watch those Clips and then at the end  after seeing those those seven films the  7 20 minute clips we actually vote on  three that we hope will become the  nominees for Best Visual Effects and a  motion picture and it's it's a terrific  process it's it's very democratic and  egalitarian and it's great to see all of  the key visual effects practitioners all  together in one night once a year
 

